#question(title: [Symmetric difference - 2], centered: true)[
  Given two sets $A$ and $B$, we define
  - $A without B = {x in A thick : thick x in.not B}$
  - $A triangle.t B = (A without B) union(B without A)$

  #v(1fr)

  Is the following equality
  $
    (A triangle.t B) triangle.t C thick = thick A triangle.t(B triangle.t C)
  $
  true for all sets $A$, $B$, and $C$?

  #v(1fr)
]
